      "id": "r20261123-a02",
      "level": "Menengah",
      "title": "Grandpa's Old Radio",
      "body": [
        "In the corner of our living room, there is an old wooden radio. It belonged to my grandpa. He bought it in 1975, and for many years it was the center of our house. Every evening, the whole family sat around it and listened to the news and old songs.",
        "When I was small, I often helped Grandpa clean the radio with a soft cloth. Sometimes the sound was full of static, and Grandpa had to move the antenna slowly until the voices became clear. He always said, 'Be patient. Good things need a little work.'",
        "Grandpa passed away two years ago, but the radio is still here. Last month, my uncle repaired it, and now it works again. When I turn it on, I feel like Grandpa is sitting next to me. That is why I will never sell it."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "wooden": "dari kayu",
        "belonged": "milik (dulu)",
        "cloth": "kain",
        "static": "desis (gangguan suara)",
        "antenna": "antena",
        "patient": "sabar",
        "passed away": "meninggal",
        "repaired": "memperbaiki"
